---
import LegalDocument from "../../components/LegalDocument.astro";
import MarketingPageShell from "../../components/MarketingPageShell.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Non-custodial Settlement — Filosign"
	description="How attached payouts work in Filosign."
>
	<MarketingPageShell>
			<LegalDocument
				title="Non-custodial Settlement"
				description="Plain-English explanation of Filosign's attached payout model, user approvals, and wallet risk."
				lastUpdated="May 2026"
			>
				<h2>Short version</h2>
				<p>
					Filosign does not custody funds. Each settlement rule is a
					document-linked record on Base: it ties a USDC payout to the same
					on-chain file registration as the agreement. You can attach a rule
					before or after signatures; execution stays permissionless once release
					conditions are met. The payer approves funds from their own wallet, and
					the validator pulls to recipients when conditions are satisfied.
				</p>

				<h2>Supported network</h2>
				<p>
					For v1 production, attached payouts run on Base. Other tokens, chains,
					fiat on-ramps, and off-ramps may rely on third-party providers and
					are not part of Filosign custody.
				</p>

				<h2>How it works</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>
						The document is registered on-chain (file registry) when sent through
						Filosign.
					</li>
					<li>
						The payer creates a settlement rule linked to that file (same
						<code>cidId</code>) in the Filosign app — before or after signing.
					</li>
					<li>The payer approves the settlement validator for the payout amount.</li>
					<li>The document is signed through the workflow.</li>
					<li>
						When the rule conditions are met, the validator can transfer approved
						funds from payer to recipient using the payer's approval.
					</li>
					<li>
						The transaction may be submitted by the Filosign relay, a user
						wallet, or another address paying gas.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>Feature access vs. fund custody</h2>
				<p>
					Filosign does not hold, pool, custody, transmit, or control your funds
					or blockchain assets. Your funds remain in your self-custodied wallet
					at all times. We cannot access, freeze, block, or reverse your funds,
					and you can transact directly with the smart contracts independent of
					Filosign.
				</p>
				<p>
					However, your access to Filosign’s software tools—such as our user
					interface, API endpoints, and transaction relay—is provided at our
					discretion. We reserve the right to suspend or restrict access to these
					platform features at any time to address security, regulatory
					compliance, abuse, or operational risks. If access to our interface is
					restricted, your funds are unaffected, and you can still interact with
					the smart contracts directly or revoke approvals using your wallet.
				</p>

				<h2>Direct contract use</h2>
				<p>
					Users may interact with contracts directly. Filosign does not guarantee
					indexing, screening, automation, or product policy enforcement for
					transactions created outside the supported app path.
				</p>

				<h2>Execution</h2>
				<p>
					A settlement transaction may be submitted by Filosign's relay, a user
					wallet, or another address when contract conditions are met. Paying gas
					does not bypass signing requirements.
				</p>

				<h2>Revoking an approval</h2>
				<p>
					Before payout execution, the payer can revoke funding by setting the
					token approval for the validator to zero from their wallet. Revocation
					cannot reverse a payout that has already executed on-chain.
				</p>

				<h2>User responsibility</h2>
				<p>
					You are responsible for wallet security, recipient correctness, token
					approval amounts, balances, taxes, invoices, reporting, sanctions
					compliance, and payout legality. Filosign cannot recover funds sent to
					the wrong address, reverse public blockchain transactions, or make a
					recipient return funds.
				</p>
			</LegalDocument>
	</MarketingPageShell>
</BaseLayout>
